<title>SWEDEN: Swedish Sodra sees pulp prices recovering in '97.</title>
<headline>Swedish Sodra sees pulp prices recovering in '97.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish non-traded forestry group Sodra Skogsagarna said on Wednesday that 1997 would be a better year for pulp prices than 1996, despite a weak start with falling prices.  </p>
<p>Sodra said in a statement that its competitive ability had strengthened and sawn timber was producing good results in terms both of price and volume.</p>
<p>&quot;SODRA has nevertheless a long way to go in order to reach the levels needed in the long-term for continued growth,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>--Stockholm newsroom +46 8 7001003</p>
</text>
